    "https://www.dewv.edu/career/enrollment-advisor/": {
      "title": "Enrollment Advisor",
      "description": "Enrollment Advisor - Davis & Elkins College Press Option+1 for screen-reader mode, Option+0 to cancel Accessibility Screen-Reader Guide, Feedback, and Issue Reporting | New window Skip to the content Davis & Elkins College Search: Search Search Academics Academics Overview Calendar Majors & Programs Pre-Professional Studies Course Catalog Directory Educational Support Booth Library Career Services Life at D&E Life at D&E Overview Residential Life Dining Services Health & Safety Morrison-Novakovic Center for Faith and Public Policy Clubs & Organizations Bookstore Admissions Admission Overview Apply Request Info Contact Us Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Tuition Costs Financial Aid Scholarships Athletics Calendar About D&E About D&E Overview Office of the President Leadership Mission, Vision & History Directory Campus Map Explore Elkins Ministry Connections Work at D&E The Senator Daily My D&E Alumni Give Back Graduates of the Last Decade (GOLD) Administrative Requests Calendar Merch & Perks Alumni Association Board Spotlight Stories Chapters Forward Magazine Current Students Self-Service Portal Forms, Tools & Resources Student Billing Registrar Course Catalog Bookstore Booth Library Career Services Commencement New & Prospective Students Enroll Visit Virtual Tour Tuition & Aid International Students Transfer Students Important Forms For Parents & Families Faculty/Staff Self-Service Portal Informer Visit Give Request Info Info Apply Home > Enrollment Advisor Enrollment Advisor Job Summary The Office of Admissions at Davis & Elkins College has an immediate opening for an Enrollment Advisor.  The role of an enrollment advisor consists of recruiting students and working with them to aid in making the decision to enroll at Davis & Elkins College.  This also includes communicating the value of a D&E education to the students and their families.  This is a 12-month position. The Enrollment Advisor will report directly to the Assistant Director of Student Recruitment. Responsibilities Travel – this position requires travel to College Fairs and High Schools Communicate with prospective college students and their families Give presentations to large and small groups Document and track contacts with recruits Perform other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Ability to manage time wisely to meet enrollment goals Work as a team member Work a non-traditional work week Ability to relate well to students, parents, scholars, faculty, staff, and others from diverse cultural backgrounds Experience in Microsoft Office, Microsoft Word, and Excel Belief in the values and mission of the College to effectively recruit qualified and retainable students Extensive knowledge of electronic communications including texting, social media, and mobile app messaging as well as phone calls Excellent oral and written communication skills A valid driver’s license Ability to operate a golf cart and college vehicles responsibly and safely Ability to pass a background check Organized reporting skills Timely responsiveness to students and supervisor A keen sense of urgency in managing tasks and time Diligent attention to detail and meticulous record-keeping Sound professional judgment and a strong sense of ethics Ability to create and maintain efficient systems and processes Ability to work independently with little supervision Ability to work effectively and successfully in a dynamic and energetic team Demonstrated ability to maintain strict confidentiality of student information Motivated learner with an ability to quickly embrace new technologies and proactively apply them Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor’s degree is required Physical Demands Must be able to lift 40 lbs. Must be able to stand and/or walk at times for long periods of time Working Environment General office setting with moderate noise level Work has deadlines, multiple interruptions, and at times, high volume Occasional evenings and weekend work required Apply Today! 100 Campus Drive, Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 100 Campus Drive Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 Contact Us Instagram Tik Tok X YouTube Flickr Facebook LinkedIn Upcoming  Events Full Calendar 11/7 Admission Open House 8 am.–1 pm. Myles Center for the Arts Myles Center for the Arts 11/11 Veterans Day All day 11/12 Capstone Day All day 11/23 Thanksgiving Break (No Classes) All day Full Calendar Explore D&E Campus Map Booth Library Flynn Planetarium Graceland Inn Bookstore Employment Contact Us Tools & Resources My D&E Portal Transcript Request Password Reset eMarketplace Media Kit Directory Compliance & Administration Consumer Information Title IX & Discrimination and Harassment ©2026 Davis & Elkins College  |  All Rights Reserved Explore D&E Search: Search We are offline - Send us an email AI Sorry, we are not online at the moment. Leave a message and we will get back to you. I agree that my personal data, provided via chat, to be processed for using live chat service by onWebChat Please give us some info to serve you better. I agree that my personal data, provided via chat, to be processed for using live chat service by onWebChat We are online - chat with us! 12:00 by onWebChat × File size larger than 50 Mb × File type not allowed × File could not be sent Send chat transcript to your email: × Transcript sent! Are you sure you want to end this chat? Thank you. We would appreciate it if you could rate this chat ★ ★ ★ ★ ★ No, thanks I agree that my personal data, provided via chat, to be processed for using live chat service Sound End chat"
