    "https://www.dewv.edu/career/line-server-dining-services/": {
      "title": "Line Server",
      "description": "Line Server - Dining Services - Davis & Elkins College Press Option+1 for screen-reader mode, Option+0 to cancel Accessibility Screen-Reader Guide, Feedback, and Issue Reporting | New window Skip to the content Davis & Elkins College Search: Search Search Academics Academics Overview Calendar Majors & Programs Pre-Professional Studies Course Catalog Directory Educational Support Booth Library Career Services Life at D&E Life at D&E Overview Residential Life Dining Services Health & Safety Morrison-Novakovic Center for Faith and Public Policy Clubs & Organizations Bookstore Admissions Admission Overview Apply Request Info Contact Us Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Tuition Costs Financial Aid Scholarships Athletics Calendar About D&E About D&E Overview Office of the President Leadership Mission, Vision & History Directory Campus Map Explore Elkins Ministry Connections Work at D&E The Senator Daily My D&E Alumni Give Back Graduates of the Last Decade (GOLD) Administrative Requests Calendar Merch & Perks Alumni Association Board Spotlight Stories Chapters Forward Magazine Current Students Self-Service Portal Forms, Tools & Resources Student Billing Registrar Course Catalog Bookstore Booth Library Career Services Commencement New & Prospective Students Enroll Visit Virtual Tour Tuition & Aid International Students Transfer Students Important Forms For Parents & Families Faculty/Staff Self-Service Portal Informer Visit Give Request Info Info Apply Home > Line Server – Dining Services Line Server – Dining Services Pay Range: $10.75 – $12.25, depending on experience Status: Full-Time or Part-Time / Hourly, Non-Exempt Responsible for serving quality food to our guests in a friendly and helpful manner under strict sanitary conditions . Responsibilities This is an overview of essential duties a more comprehensive list of expectations and responsibilities will be provided at interview Prepares service line for operation as instructed by Chef and/or Management. Serves and interacts with guests in a friendly and professional manner. Communicates with kitchen staff to maintain proper amount of food. Practice portion control guidelines. Checks quality of food items making sure they meet standards of taste, appearance and correct temperatures. Reports any substandard quality to the chef or manager on duty. Checks and logs hot holding temperatures every hour to ensure safe food handling Checks and logs cold holding temperatures every hour to ensure safe food handling Posts all necessary signage in service areas. Ensures items being served matches menu and Product Identifier labels are accurate. Follows production sheets to establish proper serving utensils. Follows cleaning schedule as provided by management using the “clean-as-you-go” techniques. Wipes down service line as needed Maintains an open line of communication with management, informing them of needed products and supplies. Follows the uniform dress code and maintains proper personal hygiene. Assists with restocking serving ware. Prepares fruits and desserts for daily service. Performs other duties as assigned by management. Responsible for other duties as assigned. Qualifications To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. ServeSafe certification obtained within six months of employment. Additional certifications required by federal, state and/or local regulations. Ability to multi-task. Ability to communicate effectively. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Standing and/or walking 100 percent of the time Occasionally lifting 25 pounds Frequently lifting 10 pounds Apply Today! 100 Campus Drive, Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 100 Campus Drive Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 Contact Us Instagram Tik Tok X YouTube Flickr Facebook LinkedIn Upcoming  Events Full Calendar 11/7 Admission Open House 8 am.–1 pm. Myles Center for the Arts Myles Center for the Arts 11/11 Veterans Day All day 11/12 Capstone Day All day 11/23 Thanksgiving Break (No Classes) All day Full Calendar Explore D&E Campus Map Booth Library Flynn Planetarium Graceland Inn Bookstore Employment Contact Us Tools & Resources My D&E Portal Transcript Request Password Reset eMarketplace Media Kit Directory Compliance & Administration Consumer Information Title IX & Discrimination and Harassment ©2026 Davis & Elkins College  |  All Rights Reserved Explore D&E Search: Search We are offline - Send us an email AI Sorry, we are not online at the moment. Leave a message and we will get back to you. I agree that my personal data, provided via chat, to be processed for using live chat service by onWebChat Please give us some info to serve you better. I agree that my personal data, provided via chat, to be processed for using live chat service by onWebChat We are online - chat with us! 12:00 by onWebChat × File size larger than 50 Mb × File type not allowed × File could not be sent Send chat transcript to your email: × Transcript sent! Are you sure you want to end this chat? Thank you. We would appreciate it if you could rate this chat ★ ★ ★ ★ ★ No, thanks I agree that my personal data, provided via chat, to be processed for using live chat service Sound End chat"
