    "https://www.dewv.edu/career/nursing-hybrid-course-instructor/": {
      "title": "Nursing Hybrid Course Instructor",
      "description": "Nursing Hybrid Course Instructor - Davis & Elkins College Skip to the content Davis & Elkins College Search: Search Search Academics Academics Overview Calendar Majors & Programs Pre-Professional Studies Course Catalog Directory Educational Support Booth Library Career Services Life at D&E Life at D&E Overview Residential Life Dining Services Health & Safety Morrison-Novakovic Center for Faith and Public Policy Clubs & Organizations Bookstore Admissions Admission Overview Apply Request Info Contact Us Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Tuition Costs Financial Aid Scholarships Athletics Calendar About D&E About D&E Overview Office of the President Leadership Mission, Vision & History Directory Campus Map Explore Elkins Ministry Connections Work at D&E The Senator Daily My D&E Alumni Give Back Graduates of the Last Decade (GOLD) Administrative Requests Calendar Merch & Perks Alumni Association Board Spotlight Stories Chapters Forward Magazine Current Students Self-Service Portal Forms, Tools & Resources Student Billing Registrar Course Catalog Bookstore Booth Library Career Services Commencement New & Prospective Students Enroll Visit Virtual Tour Tuition & Aid International Students Transfer Students Important Forms For Parents & Families Faculty/Staff Self-Service Portal Informer Visit Give Request Info Info Apply Home > Nursing Hybrid Course Instructor Nursing Hybrid Course Instructor Davis & Elkins College, a private college in the liberal arts tradition, invites applications for a full-time position within the Division of Nursing, beginning in August 2026. The position is for our new hybrid ASN and hybrid accelerated 3-year BSN programs. The successful candidate will need to be available for students, in person and online, for both evening and weekend hours. Some of the responsibilities include teaching/evaluating nursing skills in the labs, proctoring exams, conducting exam reviews, administrating makeup exams, and other duties as assigned. The faculty will spend about two-third of their time on campus, with full days on Wednesday, Saturday, and Sunday. The remaining time will be communicating with students virtually,  including evenings. Rank and salary are dependent upon qualifications and experience. Our Mission Davis & Elkins College seeks to “prepare and inspire students for success and for thoughtful engagement in the world.” To fulfill this mission, the Nursing Department is committed to provide quality education for students in the nursing program through the use of classroom and/or clinical instruction.  The department promotes an environment conducive to student growth and satisfaction, and it further contributes to the college by supporting its institutional mission, philosophy, objectives and educational goals. Job Summary Interested applicants should submit the following when applying for this role: A curriculum vitae A cover letter addressing how the applicant will fulfill the responsibilities of the position and contribute to advancing the Mission of the College Contact information for three academic or professional references Official transcripts will be required of finalists Responsibilities Participate in the development, implementation, and evaluation of the nursing curriculum Participate in the selection of learning experiences for students Promote environment conducive to student growth and satisfaction Participate in advising of assigned students Participate in textbook selection as well as other teaching material Participate in the development of course syllabi Provide classroom and clinical instruction when appropriate Utilize appropriate technology, electronic resources, and learning activities to enhance student learning Evaluate students in the classroom and clinical area Participate in recruitment and retention of students Serve on Division and College Committees Participate in College functions and activities Assume responsibility for continued professional development Assume other responsibilities as assigned by the Chair of the Division of Nursing Communicate with students and colleagues in a professional manner Establish effective working relationships with personnel from the community Qualifications Required Licensure as a registered professional nurse in West Virginia A minimum of two years’ experience as a registered professional nurse Recommended A graduate degree with a major in Nursing A bachelor’s degree with a major in Nursing and enrolled in a graduate degree program A bachelor’s degree with a major in Nursing and at least ten years of direct patient care experience in Nursing Apply Today! 100 Campus Drive, Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 100 Campus Drive Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 Contact Us Instagram Tik Tok X YouTube Flickr Facebook LinkedIn Upcoming  Events Full Calendar 11/7 Admission Open House 8 am.–1 pm. Myles Center for the Arts Myles Center for the Arts 11/11 Veterans Day All day 11/12 Capstone Day All day 11/23 Thanksgiving Break (No Classes) All day Full Calendar Explore D&E Campus Map Booth Library Flynn Planetarium Graceland Inn Bookstore Employment Contact Us Tools & Resources My D&E Portal Transcript Request Password Reset eMarketplace Media Kit Directory Compliance & Administration Consumer Information Title IX & Discrimination and Harassment ©2026 Davis & Elkins College  |  All Rights Reserved Explore D&E Search: Search"
    },
    "https://www.dewv.edu/career/public-safety-officer/": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer - Davis & Elkins College Press Option+1 for screen-reader mode, Option+0 to cancel Accessibility Screen-Reader Guide, Feedback, and Issue Reporting | New window Skip to the content Davis & Elkins College Search: Search Search Academics Academics Overview Calendar Majors & Programs Pre-Professional Studies Course Catalog Directory Educational Support Booth Library Career Services Life at D&E Life at D&E Overview Residential Life Dining Services Health & Safety Morrison-Novakovic Center for Faith and Public Policy Clubs & Organizations Bookstore Admissions Admission Overview Apply Request Info Contact Us Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Overview Tuition Costs Financial Aid Scholarships Athletics Calendar About D&E About D&E Overview Office of the President Leadership Mission, Vision & History Directory Campus Map Explore Elkins Ministry Connections Work at D&E The Senator Daily My D&E Alumni Give Back Graduates of the Last Decade (GOLD) Administrative Requests Calendar Merch & Perks Alumni Association Board Spotlight Stories Chapters Forward Magazine Current Students Self-Service Portal Forms, Tools & Resources Student Billing Registrar Course Catalog Bookstore Booth Library Career Services Commencement New & Prospective Students Enroll Visit Virtual Tour Tuition & Aid International Students Transfer Students Important Forms For Parents & Families Faculty/Staff Self-Service Portal Informer Visit Give Request Info Info Apply Home > Public Safety Officer Public Safety Officer Pay Range: $16.00-$18.00 Status: Full-Time or Part-Time / Hourly, Non-Exempt This position provides safety and security coverage to the campus of Davis and Elkins College . This person secures campus buildings & facilities, makes rounds and responds to calls . The schedule may vary depending upon the needs of the department, including evenings, nights and/or weekends. Responsibilities Respond to students/staff with safety concerns as presented and in accordance with written policies and procedures. Provide on-campus shuttle service for students, staff and faculty as requested. Conduct foot patrols every hour after buildings have been secured. Enforce campus policies as per direction of Director (e.g., parking, alcohol) Maintain appropriate records and reports. Secure buildings in manner as developed by Director. Direct traffic at events and enforce traffic/parking violations. Conduct preliminary investigations of all crimes and violations of conduct. Attend trainings or other meetings as called by the supervisor. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities High school diploma required . Must be 21 years of age, must possess a valid WV driver’s license . Working Environment Ability to communicate well with student population . Ability to work alone and be self-motivated . Must be able to work/walk on a hillside campus . Must work in inclement weather. Apply Today! 100 Campus Drive, Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 100 Campus Drive Elkins, W.Va. 26241 304-637-1900 Contact Us Instagram Tik Tok X YouTube Flickr Facebook LinkedIn Upcoming  Events Full Calendar 11/7 Admission Open House 8 am.–1 pm. Myles Center for the Arts Myles Center for the Arts 11/11 Veterans Day All day 11/12 Capstone Day All day 11/23 Thanksgiving Break (No Classes) All day Full Calendar Explore D&E Campus Map Booth Library Flynn Planetarium Graceland Inn Bookstore Employment Contact Us Tools & Resources My D&E Portal Transcript Request Password Reset eMarketplace Media Kit Directory Compliance & Administration Consumer Information Title IX & Discrimination and Harassment ©2026 Davis & Elkins College  |  All Rights Reserved Explore D&E Search: Search We are offline - Send us an email AI Sorry, we are not online at the moment. Leave a message and we will get back to you. I agree that my personal data, provided via chat, to be processed for using live chat service by onWebChat Please give us some info to serve you better. I agree that my personal